msgid "Bridging to Build Step Ordering (<code>afterBuildItem()</code>)"
msgstr ""

msgid "When a service depends on state produced by a legacy recorder (e.g., synthetic beans must be initialized), declare the dependency via `afterBuildItem()`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This resolves the producing step's nodes and creates ordering edges.\n"
"NOTE: `afterBuildItem()` is deprecated — it exists only for recorder coexistence. Once the producing recorder is converted to a service, replace with `require()` or `after()`, or drop it as appropriate."
msgstr ""

msgid "Cross-Phase Dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid "Runtime services can `require()` static-init services. The framework automatically creates a `CROSS_PHASE_PROXY` node that reads the value from the `serviceValues` map."
msgstr ""

msgid "Coexistence and Bridge APIs"
msgstr ""

msgid "During the transitional period, the `ServiceRegistrar` provides bridge APIs to allow incremental migration of extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Recorder $\\rightarrow$ Service Bridge"
msgstr ""

msgid "If you have a value produced by a legacy recorder that a new service needs to depend on, register it using `aliasRecorderValue`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Downstream services can now simply use `.require(MyLegacyValue.class)`."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Service $\\rightarrow$ Recorder Bridge"
msgstr ""

msgid "If an unconverted legacy recorder or an existing build item consumes a value that is now produced by a service, use the service-to-recorder bridge methods:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**`serviceAsRuntimeValue`**: Produces a `RuntimeValue<T>` proxy for a runtime service."
msgstr ""

msgid "**`staticInitServiceAsRuntimeValue`**: Produces a `RuntimeValue<T>` proxy for a static-init service."
msgstr ""

msgid "**`getRecorderProxy`**: Produces a bare `T` proxy (for proxyable interfaces/classes)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Common Conversion Pitfalls"
msgstr ""

msgid "ClassLoader &amp; Thread Context ClassLoader (TCCL)"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Recorder bytecode always ran with the **runtime classloader as the TCCL**. Any recorder code that captured `Thread.currentThread().getContextClassLoader()` for later use relied on that.\n"
"* After converting, ensure that the service still runs with the runtime CL as TCCL, and that captured/inherited CLs are the runtime CL (not the system `AppClassLoader`).\n"
"* Clean up threads or `ThreadLocal`s your service owns in `onStop()`; never leak the `QuarkusClassLoader`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Concrete Class Proxying"
msgstr ""

msgid "`staticInitServiceAsRecorderValue(ConcreteClass.class)` fails if the class has a non-trivial constructor. Use `staticInitServiceAsRuntimeValue()` instead — `RuntimeValue` is always proxyable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Package-Private Visibility"
msgstr ""

msgid "Lambda bytecode runs at runtime but references runtime classes directly. Package-private classes become inaccessible from the generated consolidated class. Ensure any classes referenced within the lambda are `public`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Never Reference Deployment Classes inside Service Lambdas"
msgstr ""

msgid "Always place helper methods, custom interfaces, or static factory methods inside your **runtime** module classes (which are present at runtime). Doing so inside your processor class compiles successfully but throws `NoClassDefFoundError` at runtime."
msgstr ""
